[    0s] seeds: {'arcgis_roots': 0, 'arcgis_services': 0, 'wms': 0, 'wfs': 0, 'wmts': 0, 'wcs': 0, 'hub': 0, 'ckan': 0, 'agol': 0, 'gn': 0, 'records': [{'kind': 'record', 'id': 'uk-hse-consultation-zones', 'title': 'HSE consultation zones round major hazard sites and pipelines, Great Britain (restricted, not available as data)', 'publisher': 'Health and Safety Executive (HSE)', 'publisher_type': 'central-gov', 'country': 'GB', 'abstract': "HSE draws consultation zones (inner, middle and outer) round major hazard sites and major accident hazard pipelines, and councils consult HSE on developments inside them that would bring more people near the hazard. The zones are not published as open data: HSE gives them to planning authorities through its Planning Advice Web App, and developers can use the same app to check whether a site is inside a zone (HSE says this check is free; HSE's advice on a proposal is charged). This record has no data endpoint on purpose. A check that needs these zones should say they are not available from open data, and never that there are none. A curated record for site screening (Tobler, 26 Nov 2026).", 'licence': 'Not available for re-use: HSE makes the zones available to planning authorities through its Planning Advice Web App, not as a published dataset.', 'landing_page': 'https://www.hse.gov.uk/landuseplanning/planning-advice-web-app.htm', 'bbox': [-8.65, 49.86, 1.77, 60.86], 'geometry_type': 'polygon', 'concepts_hint': ['pipeline', 'screening-zones-pack'], 'endpoints': [{'protocol': 'landing', 'url': 'https://www.hse.gov.uk/landuseplanning/planning-advice-web-app.htm', 'info': {'access': 'restricted', 'access_note': 'HSE gives the zones to planning authorities through its Planning Advice Web App; developers can check a site there themselves. Not published as data.', 'how_to_check': 'https://www.hse.gov.uk/landuseplanning/planning-advice-web-app.htm', 'nation': 'Great Britain', 'completeness': 'none', 'completeness_note': 'the zones exist for every major hazard site and pipeline, but none of them is published as data'}}], '_ctx': {'publisher': 'Health and Safety Executive (HSE)', 'publisher_type': 'central-gov', 'country': 'GB', 'seed_catalog': 'curated:screening-zones.yaml', 'discovered_via': 'curated'}}, {'kind': 'record', 'id': 'nl-rvo-natura2000', 'title': 'Natura 2000 sites, Netherlands (RVO)', 'publisher': 'Rijksdienst voor Ondernemend Nederland (RVO)', 'publisher_type': 'central-gov', 'country': 'NL', 'abstract': 'The Dutch Natura 2000 network: sites designated under the Habitats Directive (HR), the Birds Directive (VR) or both (VR+HR), on land and at sea out to the North Sea EEZ (Doggerbank, Noordzeekustzone, Voordelta). One area can have more than one feature where parts fall under different directives, so count areas by nr. naam_n2k is the site name; beschermin the directive; sitecode_h and sitecode_v the EU site codes; status the designation decision. Fields: name field naam_n2k, code field nr, class field beschermin (HR, VR, VR+HR, "HR groeve" for the four quarry sites). 209 features for 162 areas. Completeness: complete (every Dutch Natura 2000 site). Served by PDOK through OGC API Features. A curated record for Netherlands site screening (Tobler, 26 Nov 2026): the publisher\'s own service, checked to return lon/lat features for a bounding box.', 'licence': 'Public Domain Mark 1.0 (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/), as stated on the PDOK OGC API', 'landing_page': 'https://api.pdok.nl/rvo/natura2000/ogc/v1', 'bbox': [2.5, 50.7, 7.3, 55.8], 'geometry_type': 'polygon', 'concepts_hint': ['protected-area', 'screening-zones-pack'], 'endpoints': [{'protocol': 'ogc-api-features', 'url': 'https://api.pdok.nl/rvo/natura2000/ogc/v1/collections/natura2000', 'service_url': 'https://api.pdok.nl/rvo/natura2000/ogc/v1', 'capabilities': ['query'], 'info': {'name_field': 'naam_n2k', 'code_field': 'nr', 'class_field': 'beschermin', 'class_values': ['HR', 'VR', 'VR+HR', 'HR groeve'], 'nation': 'Netherlands', 'completeness': 'complete', 'completeness_note': 'every Dutch Natura 2000 site, on land and at sea. Most boundaries are the final designation; a few follow a draft decision or what was reported to the European Commission (the status field says which)', 'data_date': '2026-11-12', 'data_date_source': 'OGC API collection "updated"'}, 'check_url': 'https://api.pdok.nl/rvo/natura2000/ogc/v1/collections/natura2000/items?limit=1&f=json&bbox=5.5,52.0,6.0,52.4'}, {'protocol': 'landing', 'url': 'https://www.pdok.nl/introductie/-/article/natura-2000'}], '_ctx': {'publisher': 'Rijksdienst voor Ondernemend Nederland (RVO)', 'publisher_type': 'central-gov', 'country': 'NL', 'seed_catalog': 'curated:screening-zones.yaml', 'discovered_via': 'curated'}}, {'kind': 'record', 'id': 'us-fema-nfhl-flood-hazard-zones', 'title': 'Flood hazard zones, National Flood Hazard Layer (FEMA)', 'publisher': 'Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA)', 'publisher_type': 'central-gov', 'country': 'US', 'abstract': 'FEMA\'s effective flood hazard zones from the National Flood Hazard Layer, the digital Flood Insurance Rate Maps. FLD_ZONE is the zone (A, AE, AH, AO, VE and others are the Special Flood Hazard Area, the 1% annual chance flood; X with ZONE_SUBTY "0.2 PCT ANNUAL CHANCE FLOOD HAZARD" is the 0.2% annual chance; X alone is minimal hazard; D is undetermined). SFHA_TF is T inside the Special Flood Hazard Area. Fields: class field FLD_ZONE, subtype field ZONE_SUBTY, flag field SFHA_TF. Completeness: partial (the NFHL covers the communities with digital maps, most of the population but not every county; the service\'s layer 0, NFHL Availability, shows where). Very large: query small boxes; a count of the whole layer times out. A curated record for US site screening (Tobler, 26 Nov 2026): the publisher\'s own service, checked to return features for a bounding box (Houston).', 'licence': 'US federal government work: public domain in the US (inferred, 17 U.S.C. §105; not stated by the publisher)', 'landing_page': 'https://hazards.fema.gov/femaportal/resources/flood_map_svc.htm', 'bbox': [-179.2, -14.6, 179.8, 71.4], 'geometry_type': 'polygon', 'concepts_hint': ['flood-risk', 'screening-zones-pack'], 'endpoints': [{'protocol': 'arcgis-mapserver', 'url': 'https://hazards.fema.gov/arcgis/rest/services/public/NFHL/MapServer/28', 'service_url': 'https://hazards.fema.gov/arcgis/rest/services/public/NFHL/MapServer', 'capabilities': ['query', 'render'], 'info': {'class_field': 'FLD_ZONE', 'subtype_field': 'ZONE_SUBTY', 'flag_field': 'SFHA_TF', 'class_values': ['A', 'AE', 'AH', 'AO', 'AR', 'A99', 'V', 'VE', 'X', 'D', 'OPEN WATER', 'AREA NOT INCLUDED'], 'nation': 'United States', 'completeness': 'partial', 'completeness_note': 'communities with digital flood maps (NFHL); layer 0 of the service, NFHL Availability, shows where the NFHL has data. Elsewhere older paper maps may apply'}, 'check_url': 'https://hazards.fema.gov/arcgis/rest/services/public/NFHL/MapServer/28/query?geometry=-95.4,29.7,-95.3,29.8&geometryType=esriGeometryEnvelope&inSR=4326&outFields=FLD_ZONE&returnGeometry=false&resultRecordCount=1&f=json', 'manual_check': "checked by hand: probe round 54, 26 Nov 2026, a Houston box query returned zones X and AE. hazards.fema.gov disallows automated checks in robots.txt and refuses or times out GitHub's runners"}, {'protocol': 'landing', 'url': 'https://hazards.fema.gov/femaportal/resources/flood_map_svc.htm', 'manual_check': "checked by hand: probe round 54, 26 Nov 2026, a Houston box query returned zones X and AE. hazards.fema.gov disallows automated checks in robots.txt and refuses or times out GitHub's runners"}], '_ctx': {'publisher': 'Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA)', 'publisher_type': 'central-gov', 'country': 'US', 'seed_catalog': 'curated:screening-zones.yaml', 'discovered_via': 'curated'}}, {'kind': 'record', 'id': 'us-epa-sole-source-aquifers', 'title': 'Sole Source Aquifers (EPA)', 'publisher': 'U.S. Environmental Protection Agency', 'publisher_type': 'central-gov', 'country': 'US', 'abstract': "Aquifers EPA has designated as the sole or principal source of drinking water for the area above them (at least 50% of the drinking water used there), with their recharge and streamflow source areas where EPA regions have mapped them. Federally funded projects inside one are reviewed by EPA (Safe Drinking Water Act, section 1424(e)). SSA_NAME is the aquifer; SSA_ID its id; FR_ID the Federal Register notice of the designation. Fields: name field SSA_NAME, code field SSA_ID. 93 features. Completeness: complete (every designated Sole Source Aquifer). From EPA's NEPAssist service. A curated record for US site screening (Tobler, 26 Nov 2026): the publisher's own service, checked to return features for a bounding box.", 'licence': 'Public domain: "Unless otherwise specified, all data produced by the U.S EPA is by default in the public domain and is not subject to domestic copyright protection under 17 U.S.C. § 105." (https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/)', 'landing_page': 'https://www.epa.gov/dwssa/map-sole-source-aquifer-locations', 'bbox': [-158.15, 13.41, 144.96, 48.59], 'geometry_type': 'polygon', 'concepts_hint': ['groundwater-protection', 'screening-zones-pack'], 'endpoints': [{'protocol': 'arcgis-mapserver', 'url': 'https://geopub.epa.gov/ArcGIS/rest/services/NEPAssist/Water/MapServer/6', 'service_url': 'https://geopub.epa.gov/ArcGIS/rest/services/NEPAssist/Water/MapServer', 'capabilities': ['query', 'render'], 'info': {'name_field': 'SSA_NAME', 'code_field': 'SSA_ID', 'nation': 'United States', 'completeness': 'complete', 'completeness_note': 'every designated Sole Source Aquifer'}, 'check_url': 'https://geopub.epa.gov/ArcGIS/rest/services/NEPAssist/Water/MapServer/6/query?where=1%3D1&returnCountOnly=true&f=json'}, {'protocol': 'landing', 'url': 'https://www.epa.gov/dwssa/map-sole-source-aquifer-locations'}], '_ctx': {'publisher': 'U.S. Environmental Protection Agency', 'publisher_ty